  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The hand has 6 Plains and a Thriving Heath — all lands, no spells. While mulliganing is correct, a 7-land hand is an obvious mulligan that the player correctly identified. However, looking more carefully, the player chose True (mulligan), which is the right call. This is not a blunder.",
      "action_taken": "Mulligan the 7-land hand",
      "better_line": "Mulligan is correct",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "GPT52 Brewer",
      "decision_index": 1,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mountain instead of Thriving Moor when there's nothing to cast this turn anyway. Thriving Moor enters tapped (no cost since nothing costs 1 mana) and would provide both black and red mana from a single land, improving color flexibility for future turns.",
      "action_taken": "Played Mountain",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Moor choosing Red, giving access to both B and R from one land with no downside since nothing can be cast this turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 12,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 6,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Distinguished Conjurer was chosen over Lightwalker, despite Lightwalker having strong synergy with Basri's Solidarity already in hand. Playing Lightwalker here sets up a Turn 4 line of Plains + Basri's Solidarity to create a 3/2 flying threat, which is a very aggressive and efficient curve. Distinguished Conjurer's incremental life gain is less impactful than establishing an evasive clock.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Distinguished Conjurer (1/2 with ETB lifegain triggers)",
      "better_line": "Cast Lightwalker, then next turn play Plains and cast Basri's Solidarity to make it a 3/2 flier - a much more proactive and threatening development.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 20,
      "player": "GPT52 Brewer",
      "decision_index": 10,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Discarded Finishing Blow (their only hard removal) instead of Storm Fleet Pyromancer. Finishing Blow is instant-speed unconditional removal for creatures and planeswalkers, which is premium in Limited. Storm Fleet Pyromancer is a 5-mana 3/2 with conditional 2 damage - a reasonable card but less irreplaceable than hard removal.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Finishing Blow",
      "better_line": "Discard Storm Fleet Pyromancer instead, keeping Finishing Blow as a versatile answer to opponent's threats",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 37,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 13,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attacked with just Distinguished Conjurer for 1 damage instead of first playing Plains, casting Siege Striker (2W), and attacking with Siege Striker while tapping Distinguished Conjurer to pump it. Siege Striker as a 2/2 double striker would deal 4 damage vs the 1 damage from Conjurer alone. The opponent has only 1 Mountain untapped and no blockers, so there's minimal risk.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with Distinguished Conjurer alone for 1 damage before playing land or casting creatures.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains precombat, cast Siege Striker (2W), then attack with Siege Striker tapping Distinguished Conjurer to make it a 2/2 double striker for 4 damage through an empty board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 40,
      "player": "GPT52 Brewer",
      "decision_index": 14,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mountain over Thriving Moor (or Swamp) wastes an opportunity to add black mana access. With 2 Mountains already providing red, a third red source is redundant. The player has Village Rites (B) in hand and needs black mana. Thriving Moor enters tapped but that doesn't matter this turn since nothing useful costs 3 or less. It would provide both black and a chosen color (red), giving strictly better color flexibility.",
      "action_taken": "Played Mountain as third land, adding redundant red mana without gaining black access.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Moor (choosing red) to gain access to both black mana (for Village Rites and future black spells) and red mana, at no cost since it entering tapped doesn't matter this turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 73,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 24,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Played a 4th Mountain when they already had 3 red sources, missing the opportunity to enable Village Rites ({B}) by playing a Swamp instead. The extra Mountain provides redundant red mana while a Swamp would open up a new spell option.",
      "action_taken": "Played Mountain as their land for the turn",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp to enable Village Rites (if a sacrifice opportunity arises) and diversify mana base. They already have 3 Mountains which is more than enough red for their 5-drops.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 111,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 32,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player passed priority in their precombat main phase without playing a land, despite having 4 land options in hand (3 Swamps and a Thriving Moor) and a land drop remaining. They have 4 Mountains in play and need to get to 5 mana to cast Plundering Predator or Storm Fleet Pyromancer. Playing Thriving Moor (choosing red) this turn would let them have 5 mana next turn. Even playing a Swamp would progress toward casting Storm Fleet Pyromancer (4R). Skipping the land drop wastes a turn of mana development.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing a land in precombat main phase.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Moor (choosing red) to have 5 mana sources available next turn, enabling Plundering Predator or Storm Fleet Pyromancer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 155,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 45,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "QwCdr Stats passed priority in the postcombat main phase with a land drop remaining and 4 land cards in hand (3 Swamps and a Thriving Moor). They have Plundering Predator (4R) and Storm Fleet Pyromancer (4R) in hand, both costing 5 mana. With only 4 Mountains in play, playing a land this turn would get them to 5 mana next turn, enabling these creatures. Passing here wastes a land drop and delays their curve by a full turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing a land, ending the turn with only 4 lands.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Moor (choosing red) to have 5 mana sources next turn, enabling Plundering Predator or Storm Fleet Pyromancer on curve.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 172,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 50,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Passed priority in precombat main with 3 untapped Plains and Siege Striker in hand. Siege Striker with double strike could attack this turn while tapping other creatures for significant pump damage. With opponent at 14 life and Kari Zev tapped, this was an excellent time to deploy the threat. Even Trusty Retriever at 4 mana would be playable next turn after the new land enters untapped.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting anything, wasting 3 available mana.",
      "better_line": "Cast Siege Striker (2W), then go to combat. Attack with Siege Striker and one flyer, tapping remaining creatures to pump Siege Striker. For example, attack with Siege Striker + Lightwalker, tap Conjurer and Overseer to make Siege Striker a 3/3 double strike dealing 6 + 3 flying = 9 damage, putting opponent to 5.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 180,
      "player": "GPT52 Brewer",
      "decision_index": 53,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 6 life facing lethal in the air next turn (two 3/2 flyers), QwCdr Stats passed on their land drop when they could play a Swamp and cast Crypt Lurker (3/4) to at least have a blocker and potentially draw a card by sacrificing Kari Zev. Missing the land drop means they can't cast any spells this turn, wasting a critical turn when they're about to die.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing a land, missing the land drop entirely.",
      "better_line": "Play a Swamp, then cast Crypt Lurker (3B) using 3 Mountains + 1 Swamp. On ETB, sacrifice Kari Zev to draw a card, getting a 3/4 body and an extra card to potentially find an answer to the lethal flyers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 199,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 59,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "QwCdr Stats passed priority in their postcombat main phase without playing a land. They have 4 untapped Mountains, 1 land drop remaining, and 3 Swamps plus a Thriving Moor in hand. Playing a land here is free and would give them 5 mana next turn, enabling Crypt Lurker (4 mana) or Storm Fleet Pyromancer (5 mana) or Plundering Predator (5 mana). By not playing a land, they delay their ability to cast their higher-cost creatures by a turn, which is significant when they're at 6 life facing a board of buffed fliers and creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing a land, ending the turn with only 4 lands on the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Play a Swamp (or Thriving Moor) to have 5 lands available next turn, enabling casting of Plundering Predator or Storm Fleet Pyromancer on turn 15.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 216,
      "player": "QwCdr Stats",
      "decision_index": 65,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Village Rites instead of a redundant Swamp. With 3 Swamps and a Thriving Moor in hand, a third Swamp is redundant. Village Rites could sacrifice Kari Zev (or Ragavan token) for 1 mana to draw 2 cards, which is critical when at 6 life facing lethal flyers and needing to find answers.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Village Rites",
